/-!
# Reciprocity over a number field for a subcyclotomic cyclic algebra

Reciprocity over the rationals is known for a cyclic algebra split by a totally real subfield of
the field of the primitive roots of unity of an odd prime.  The same construction can be carried
out over an arbitrary number field: the roots of unity generate an extension of the base, the
totally real subfield generates a subextension of it, and a unit of the base gives a cyclic
algebra split by that subextension.  Its total invariant is compared with the total invariant of
the corresponding algebra over the rationals, taken at the norm of the unit, and the comparison is
made place by place over each rational prime.

Away from the conductor both invariants are read from the same exponent of a power of the chosen
generator of the roots of unity, weighted by the residue degree and the value of the coefficient;
the residue degrees above a rational prime add up with the values to the value of the norm, so the
fibre multiplies out to the invariant below.  At the conductor both invariants are read from a
power residue congruence in the residue ring, and the reduction of a norm is the product of the
norms of the reductions, so the exponents above the prime add up to the exponent below it.  At the
infinite places both invariants vanish, since both splitting fields are generated by a totally
real field.

The first half of that computation is packaged as a single statement over an arbitrary base, so
that the two sides of the comparison at the conductor are two instances of one lemma: the
invariant of the algebra at the place of the conductor is named by an exponent, and that same
exponent names the coefficient as a power residue there.

## Main results

* `InverseGalois.CFT.exists_mk_pow_eq_placeInvariant_conductor`: **the invariant at the place of
  the conductor of a cyclic algebra split by a subfield of the field of the primitive roots of
  unity of an odd prime is named by the exponent expressing the coefficient as a power residue.**
* `InverseGalois.CFT.totalInvariant_cyclicBrauerHom_base_subcyclotomic`: **the total invariant of a
  cyclic algebra over a number field split by a subfield of the field of the primitive roots of
  unity of an odd prime, with an integral coefficient that is a unit above the prime, vanishes.**

## Tags

number field, cyclotomic field, Brauer group, local invariant, total invariant, cyclic algebra,
power residue symbol, reciprocity, class field theory
-/

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000

namespace InverseGalois.CFT

